I must say I am surprised on the information about the Ohio Steve Brack
case. We have redone our policies several times to make them more clear.
We were told that any kind of computer abuse type of case sent to student
affairs must be handled the same as in a court of law (if a court of law
would not find the evidence as legal proof then there is no bases for the
case). Likewise such terms as public domain have been changed so that
any person whether a regular computer user or not would understand without
a doubt the meaning of the rule. Not knowing all details of the case I will
mention the first offense is usually handled with removing access for
a week or maybe two. Second offense a semester, further problems a year.
Of course these depend of the level of abuse. I know we have never
removed a student from school on a abuse case and we have some serious
cases. We have also been told that if a student is not satisfied with the
handling of the case at student affairs they may get a lawyer and take
the case to a regular court of law.

