umm, not quite so simple.  a VERY important question becomes whether or
not there was any expectation of privacy on the system.  ALSO, keep in
mind that the ECPA, being a FEDERAL law, has only limited applicability
for an entity that is solely within a single state.

AND... even though the ECPA may cover this issue, the question comes up
whether it will make any difference inthe final reult.  remember, the
desire he (presumably) is to prevent or overturn any charges/convictions
of the students.  The Bush/Reagan Supreme Court has pretty much voided the
exclusionary rule, so even if the search was illegal, it may still stand.

